1
00:00:03,303 --> 00:00:06,805
(Q1（Table）) Tim: Good morning.&nbsp; You're through to the tourist information office,

2
00:00:06,805 --> 00:00:08,923
Tim speaking.How can I help you?

3
00:00:08,923 --> 00:00:10,303
Jean: Oh hello.&nbsp;

4
00:00:10,303 --> 00:00:14,393
Could you give me some information about next month's festival, please?

5
00:00:14,393 --> 00:00:17,582
My family and I will be staying in the town that week.

6
00:00:17,582 --> 00:00:18,908
Tim: Of course.&nbsp;

7
00:00:18,908 --> 00:00:23,639
Well it starts with a concert on the afternoon of the 17th.

8
00:00:23,639 --> 00:00:25,374
Jean: Oh I heard about that.&nbsp;

9
00:00:25,374 --> 00:00:29,054
The orchestra and singers come from the USA, don't they?

10
00:00:29,054 --> 00:00:30,802
Tim: They're from Canada.&nbsp;

11
00:00:30,802 --> 00:00:33,440
They're very popular over there.

12
00:00:33,440 --> 00:00:39,433
They're going to perform a number of well-known pieces that will appeal to children as well as adults.

13
00:00:39,433 --> 00:00:40,824
Jean: That sounds good.&nbsp;

14
00:00:40,824 --> 00:00:43,556
My whole family are interested in music.

15
00:00:43,556 --> 00:00:51,904
Tim: The next day, the 18th, there's a performance by a ballet company called Eustatis.&nbsp;Jean: Sorry?&nbsp;

16
00:00:51,904 --> 00:00:59,134
[Q1答案句（字母拼写）] Tim: The name is spelt E-U-S-T-A-T-I-S.&nbsp;

17
00:00:59,134 --> 00:01:03,066
(Q2) They appeared in last year's festival, and went down very well.

18
00:01:03,066 --> 00:01:06,911
Again, their programme is designed for all ages.

19
00:01:06,911 --> 00:01:07,823
Jean: Good.&nbsp;

20
00:01:07,823 --> 00:01:09,539
I expect we'll go to that.

21
00:01:09,539 --> 00:01:15,324
I hope there's going to be a play during the festival, a comedy, ideally.

22
00:01:15,324 --> 00:01:16,492
Tim: You're in luck!&nbsp;

23
00:01:16,492 --> 00:01:23,413
On the 19th and 20th a local amateur group are performing one written by a member of the group.&nbsp;

24
00:01:23,413 --> 00:01:36,196
[Q2答案句：跟空前 Jemima，+ 疑似答案记录  is good（听句首）] It's called Jemima. That will be on in the town hall.&nbsp; They've already performed it two or three times.I haven't seen it myself, but the review in the local paper was very good.

25
00:01:36,196 --> 00:01:38,671
(Q3) Jean: And is it suitable for children?&nbsp;

26
00:01:38,671 --> 00:01:46,517
Tim: Yes, in fact it's aimed more at children than at adults, so both performances are in the afternoon.&nbsp;

27
00:01:46,517 --> 00:01:54,676
[Q3答案句： 疑似答案记录，+ performance=show， 确定答案] Jean: And what about dance?&nbsp; Will there be any performances?Tim: Yes, also on the 20th, but in the evening.&nbsp;

28
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,000


29
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,000


30
00:01:54,676 --> 00:02:02,017
A professional company is putting on a show of modern pieces, with electronic music by young composers.

31
00:02:02,017 --> 00:02:03,022
Jean: Uh-huh.&nbsp;

32
00:02:03,022 --> 00:02:12,032
(Q4) [Q4答案句] Tim: The show is about how people communicate, or fail to communicate, with each other, so it's got the rather strange name, Chat.

33
00:02:12,032 --> 00:02:17,844
Jean: I suppose that's because that's something we do both face to face and online.&nbsp;

34
00:02:17,844 --> 00:02:21,729
Tim: That's right.&nbsp;

35
00:02:21,729 --> 00:02:25,957
(Q5（notes）) Tim: Now there are also some workshops and other activities.&nbsp;

36
00:02:25,957 --> 00:02:32,309
They'll all take place at least once every day, so everyone who wants to take part will have a chance.

37
00:02:32,309 --> 00:02:33,142
Jean: Good.&nbsp;

38
00:02:33,142 --> 00:02:36,407
We're particularly interested in cookery

39
00:02:36,407 --> 00:02:39,989
you don't happen to have a cookery workshop, do you?

40
00:02:39,989 --> 00:02:46,306
[Q5答案句： healthy， 词组类 语序调换] Tim: We certainly do.&nbsp; It's going to focus on how to make food part of a health lifestyle,

41
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,000
⭐

42
00:02:46,306 --> 00:02:53,950
and it'll show that even sweet things like cakes can contain much less sugar than they usually do.

43
00:02:53,950 --> 00:02:56,006
Jean: That might be worth going to.&nbsp;

44
00:02:56,006 --> 00:02:59,446
(Q6) We're trying to encourage our children to cook.

45
00:02:59,446 --> 00:03:07,254
[Q6答案句] Tim: Another workshop is just for children, and that's on creating posters to reflect the history of the town.&nbsp;

46
00:03:07,254 --> 00:03:15,561
The aim is to make children aware of how both the town and people's lives have changed over the centuries.

47
00:03:15,561 --> 00:03:19,037
The results will be exhibited in the community centre.

48
00:03:19,037 --> 00:03:25,372
(Q7) Then the other workshop is in toy-making, and that's for adults only.

49
00:03:25,372 --> 00:03:27,123
Jean: Oh, why's that?&nbsp;

50
00:03:27,123 --> 00:03:33,256
[Q7答案句] Tim: Because it involves carpentry – participants will be making toys out of wood,&nbsp;

51
00:03:33,256 --> 00:03:37,801
so there will be a lot of sharp chisels and other tools around.

52
00:03:37,801 --> 00:03:40,736
Jean: It makes sense to keep children away from it.&nbsp;

53
00:03:40,736 --> 00:03:42,097
Tim: Exactly.&nbsp;

54
00:03:42,097 --> 00:03:46,329
(Q8) Now let me tell you about some of the outdoor activities.

55
00:03:46,329 --> 00:03:49,140
There will be supervised wild swimming …

56
00:03:49,140 --> 00:03:50,716
Jean: Wild swimming?&nbsp;

57
00:03:50,716 --> 00:03:52,105
What's that?

58
00:03:52,105 --> 00:03:56,960
[Q8干扰项 natural waters不符合字数要求] Tim: It just means swimming in natural waters, rather than a swimming pool.&nbsp;

59
00:03:56,960 --> 00:04:06,380
[Q8答案句 疑似答案记录 +代词指代] Jean: Oh OK.&nbsp; In a lake, for instance.Tim: Yes, there's a beautiful one just outside the town, and that will be the venue for the swimming.&nbsp;

60
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,000


61
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,000
⭐

62
00:04:06,380 --> 00:04:11,359
There will be lifeguards on duty, so it's suitable for all ages.

63
00:04:11,359 --> 00:04:16,669
(Q9) And finally, there will be a walk in some nearby woods every day.

64
00:04:16,669 --> 00:04:20,235
[Q9答案句] The leader is an expert on insects.

65
00:04:20,235 --> 00:04:25,342
He'll show some that live in the woods, and how important they are for the environment.

66
00:04:25,342 --> 00:04:30,238
So there are going to be all sorts of different things to do during the festival.

67
00:04:30,238 --> 00:04:32,064
Jean: There certainly are.&nbsp;

68
00:04:32,064 --> 00:04:39,239
(Q10) [Q10答案句] Tim: If you'd like to read about how the preparations for the festival are going, the festival organizer is keeping a blog.&nbsp;

69
00:04:39,239 --> 00:04:44,091
Just search online for the festival website, and you'll find it.

70
00:04:44,091 --> 00:04:47,475
Jean: Well, thank you very much for all the information.&nbsp;

71
00:04:47,475 --> 00:04:48,365
Tim: You're welcome.&nbsp;

72
00:04:48,365 --> 00:04:49,124
Goodbye.

73
00:04:49,124 --> 00:04:51,624
Jean: Goodbye.&nbsp;

